# {{.ProviderName}} Provider

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

One provider instance configures one store; use provider aliases for several stores. The provider covers store configuration (metafield and metaobject definitions, markets, locations, shipping, menus, locales, policies and more) and, as volatile types, some content. App configuration, themes and transactional records (orders, payments and the like) are out of scope: use `shopify.app.toml` with the Shopify CLI and theme tooling for those.

To bring an existing store under Terraform, see [Importing an existing store](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/pflege-de-labs/shopify/latest/docs/guides/importing-an-existing-store).

